at conflicts with current inventory or fails contract validation.","id":"AC-REQ-8.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is the contract-declared 409 or 422 and the response contains the contract ApiError fields.","when":"The client sends POST /api/feeding-events."},{"given":"A feeding event has been successfully saved and the App PostgreSQL database is available.","id":"AC-REQ-8.5","level":"api","then":"The response contains the saved event and corresponding stock and lot totals.","when":"The API process restarts and the client reads the event and inventory."}],"ears":"When an authorized client records, corrects, or voids a feeding event, the Feedlot API shall persist the event and return its contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","Q-1"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and operational feeding, performance, and inventory data with supported filters.","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response rows and summary match the filters, or the response contains a CSV file derived only from the authorized filtered rows.","when":"The client sends GET /api/reports/operational or GET /api/reports/operational/export."},{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a required date range plus optional breed, sex, or pen filters.","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response rows contain contract-defined ADG, feed, FCR, cost-of-gain, and energy fields for matching lots.","when":"The client sends GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain."},{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a valid feed-to-gain date range, supported filters, and format csv or pdf.","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response file artifact has contentType and content corresponding to the requested format and filtered authorized rows.","when":"The client sends GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain/export."},{"given":"A client omits a required feed-to-gain date or supplies an export format outside the contract enum.","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the response error code is VALIDATION_ERROR.","when":"The client sends a feed-to-gain report or export request."},{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies supported profitability horizon, breed, penId, or roiStatus filters.","id":"AC-REQ-9.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains authorized matching profitability rows and canViewProfitability where declared, or a CSV file with those filtered authorized rows.","when":"The client sends GET /api/reports/profitability or GET /api/reports/profitability/export."}],"ears":"When an authorized client requests an operational, feed-to-gain, or profitability report or export, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined permission-filtered rows, calculations, summaries, and requested export artifacts.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-1"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and sample records may be absent, not yet loaded, or already loaded.","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response loaded, recordCount, records, and load status distinguish an empty set, a successful load, and already_loaded without duplicating records.","when":"The client sends GET /api/sample-data or POST /api/sample-data/load."},{"given":"A client has a valid bearer token and sends reset or replacement first without required confirmation and then with explicit confirmation.","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"api","then":"The unconfirmed response status is the contract-declared 422 or 409, and the confirmed response has the completed operation status and resulting recordCount.","when":"The client sends POST /api/sample-data/reset or POST /api/sample-data/replace."}],"ears":"When an authorized client reads, loads, resets, or replaces sample records, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined sample status and records, avoid duplicate loading, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-1"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is configured with an App PostgreSQL connection and a client successfully creates or updates a contract resource.","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains the saved value and the returned record has the same id and field values as the successful write response.","when":"The API process restarts and the client retrieves the resource through its contract-defined read operation."},{"given":"The API is configured with a connection string named App and a successful contract write has completed.","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"api","then":"A row with the values written by the request is present in the App database.","when":"A test queries the configured PostgreSQL database for the affected entity."},{"given":"The API starts with a configured App PostgreSQL connection.","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"api","then":"A row exists in PostgreSQL for each persisted record type required by the implemented contract operations.","when":"Startup creates the database schema."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":9,"lineStart":8,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\"App\")\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_1»\")));"},{"lineEnd":22,"lineStart":20,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();"},{"lineEnd":7,"lin